From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_hwifi: demote DSP and WM firmware version banners from dev_err to dev_info

Printing loaded DSP and WM firmware versions and build timestamps during probe
is informational; real firmware load errors and failures continue to use
dev_err().

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_dsp.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_dsp.c
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@
 	hdr = (const struct mcu_fw_trailer *)(fw->data + fw->size -
 					sizeof(*hdr));
 
-	dev_err(dev->dev, "DSP Firmware Version: %.10s, Build Time: %.15s\n",
+	dev_info(dev->dev, "DSP Firmware Version: %.10s, Build Time: %.15s\n",
 		 hdr->fw_ver, hdr->build_date);
 
 	ret = mcu_dsp_send_ram_firmware(dev, hdr, fw->data);
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	dev_err(dev->dev, "HW/SW Version: 0x%x, Build Time: %.16s\n",
+	dev_info(dev->dev, "HW/SW Version: 0x%x, Build Time: %.16s\n",
 		 be32_to_cpu(hdr->hw_sw_ver), hdr->build_date);
 
 	n_region = be32_to_cpu(hdr->desc.n_region);
